SELECT '95f3e650-f1a7-4e0c-b0ca-d2e609ac464e',id,user_id,'user','revision','Automated acceptance feedback from the outline review: retain the 20-slide teaching sequence and the existing useful examples. (1) On slide 7 add 5x5 and 7x7 input-size presets: with Cin=3, Cout=4, kernel=3, stride=1 and no padding, output spatial size changes 3x3 to 5x5 while output channels stay 4 and parameter count stays 112. (2) On slides 8 and 9 allow the upstream gradient to be set to 1. Test ReLU at -2, 0 and 3 with backward outputs 0, 0 and 1; test pooling on [[1,3],[2,4]] with max=4, average=2.5, max gradient only at bottom-right, and average gradient 0.25 in each cell. Keep the original alternative examples as well. (3) On slide 14 or 17 provide a runnable finite-difference check of the complete CNN cross-entropy loss for at least one convolution weight, convolution bias, classifier weight and classifier bias. Use epsilon=1e-5 away from ReLU kinks and assert maximum absolute error below 1e-5; a linear sum(Z) example alone does not establish this. (4) Describe ReLU at zero and tied max pooling as nondifferentiable points with a chosen backward convention, rather than saying a classical derivative is nonunique. Keep the stated zero-at-ReLU and first-maximum tie rules. Show the scientific explanations naturally on the lesson; keep acceptance-test terminology in the report.','[]','pending',CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER) * 1000,CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
